{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Knot.FiveTwoNinthPower","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Knot.FiveTwoNinthPower","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Knot.FiveTwoShapeBounds"],"declarations":32,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FiveTwoNinthPower.all_angles_gt_two_pi_div_nine","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FiveTwoNinthPower.all_angles_gt_two_pi_div_nine","kind":"theorem","line":388,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FiveTwoNinthPower.lean#L388-L397","doc":"**All three dihedral angles exceed `2π/9`** — so the chord bound's\nhypothesis holds for the minimum, whichever it is. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FiveTwoNinthPower.pi_div_four_lt_angle₂","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FiveTwoNinthPower.pi_div_four_lt_angle₂","kind":"theorem","line":380,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FiveTwoNinthPower.lean#L380-L386","doc":"**`π/4 < angle₂`** — from the angle sum, `angle₁ < π/2` and `angle₃ < π/4`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FiveTwoNinthPower.angle₁_lt_pi_div_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FiveTwoNinthPower.angle₁_lt_pi_div_two","kind":"theorem","line":371,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FiveTwoNinthPower.lean#L371-L377","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FiveTwoNinthPower.pi_div_four_lt_angle₁","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FiveTwoNinthPower.pi_div_four_lt_angle₁","kind":"theorem","line":355,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FiveTwoNinthPower.lean#L355-L368","doc":"**`π/4 < angle₁`**, from `Im y₁ > Re y₁`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FiveTwoNinthPower.fiveTwoShape_im_gt_re","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FiveTwoNinthPower.fiveTwoShape_im_gt_re","kind":"theorem","line":343,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FiveTwoNinthPower.lean#L343-L352","doc":"`Im y₁ > Re y₁` — reduced, this is `2t² + 4 > 0`, unconditional. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FiveTwoNinthPower.fiveTwoShape_re_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FiveTwoNinthPower.fiveTwoShape_re_pos","kind":"theorem","line":339,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FiveTwoNinthPower.lean#L339-L340","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FiveTwoNinthPower.two_pi_div_nine_lt_angle₃","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FiveTwoNinthPower.two_pi_div_nine_lt_angle₃","kind":"theorem","line":323,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FiveTwoNinthPower.lean#L323-L329","doc":"**The 5₂ tetrahedron's third dihedral angle exceeds `2π/9`.**\n\n`qou-52ch`'s chord bound needs this of the *smallest* angle; `angle₃` is the\nsmallest numerically (`0.7039` against `1.0300` and `1.4077`), but that ordering\nis not proved here — see the module header. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FiveTwoNinthPower.zz_arg_eq_angle₃","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FiveTwoNinthPower.zz_arg_eq_angle₃","kind":"theorem","line":318,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FiveTwoNinthPower.lean#L318-L321","doc":"`arg z` is the third dihedral angle. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FiveTwoNinthPower.two_pi_div_nine_lt_zz_arg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FiveTwoNinthPower.two_pi_div_nine_lt_zz_arg","kind":"theorem","line":285,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FiveTwoNinthPower.lean#L285-L311","doc":"**`2π/9 < arg z`** — the smallest dihedral angle of the 5₂ tetrahedron\nexceeds `2π/9`.\n\nThis is the inequality the Rivin-concavity chord bound needs, and it is reached\nwithout a single value of a transcendental function: `z³ = z − 1` gives\n`z⁹ = −3z² + 4z − 2`, whose imaginary part is positive precisely when\n`Re z < 2/3`, which is the quadratic `−3t² + 6t − 2 > 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FiveTwoNinthPower.zz_pow_nine_arg_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FiveTwoNinthPower.zz_pow_nine_arg_pos","kind":"theorem","line":276,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FiveTwoNinthPower.lean#L276-L282","doc":"`0 < arg (z⁹)`: nonneg from `Im (z⁹) > 0`, and nonzero because a zero\nargument forces a zero imaginary part. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FiveTwoNinthPower.pi_div_six_lt_zz_arg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FiveTwoNinthPower.pi_div_six_lt_zz_arg","kind":"theorem","line":254,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FiveTwoNinthPower.lean#L254-L266","doc":"`π/6 < arg z`, from `√3·Im z > Re z` — i.e. `Im/Re > tan (π/6) = 1/√3`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FiveTwoNinthPower.zz_arg_lt_pi_div_four","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FiveTwoNinthPower.zz_arg_lt_pi_div_four","kind":"theorem","line":246,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FiveTwoNinthPower.lean#L246-L251","doc":"`arg z < π/4`, from `Im z < Re z`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FiveTwoNinthPower.zz_arg_eq_arctan","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FiveTwoNinthPower.zz_arg_eq_arctan","kind":"theorem","line":237,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FiveTwoNinthPower.lean#L237-L243","doc":"`arg z = arctan (Im z / Re z)`, valid because `Re z > 0` puts `arg z` in\n`(−π/2, π/2)` where `arctan` inverts `tan`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FiveTwoNinthPower.sqrt_three_mul_zz_im_gt_re","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FiveTwoNinthPower.sqrt_three_mul_zz_im_gt_re","kind":"theorem","line":219,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FiveTwoNinthPower.lean#L219-L234","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FiveTwoNinthPower.zz_im_lt_re","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FiveTwoNinthPower.zz_im_lt_re","kind":"theorem","line":208,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FiveTwoNinthPower.lean#L208-L217","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FiveTwoNinthPower.zz_im_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FiveTwoNinthPower.zz_im_eq","kind":"theorem","line":191,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FiveTwoNinthPower.lean#L191-L201","doc":"**`Im z = t·√(3t² − 4t + 8) / 2`** — via `‖y₁‖² = 1/t` again. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FiveTwoNinthPower.disc_pos'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FiveTwoNinthPower.disc_pos'","kind":"theorem","line":187,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FiveTwoNinthPower.lean#L187-L189","doc":"The discriminant is positive, so its square root behaves. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FiveTwoNinthPower.zz_re_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FiveTwoNinthPower.zz_re_pos","kind":"theorem","line":184,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FiveTwoNinthPower.lean#L184-L185","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FiveTwoNinthPower.zz_pow_nine_im_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FiveTwoNinthPower.zz_pow_nine_im_pos","kind":"theorem","line":163,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FiveTwoNinthPower.lean#L163-L175","doc":"**`0 < Im (z⁹)`.**\n\n`z⁹ = −3z² + 4z − 2`, so `Im (z⁹) = Im z · (4 − 6 Re z)`, and both factors are\npositive.  No degree-9 expansion, and no value of any transcendental. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FiveTwoNinthPower.zz_re_lt_two_thirds","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FiveTwoNinthPower.zz_re_lt_two_thirds","kind":"theorem","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FiveTwoNinthPower.lean#L156-L159","doc":"**`Re z < 2/3`** — equivalent to the reduced quadratic of §2. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FiveTwoNinthPower.zz_re_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FiveTwoNinthPower.zz_re_eq","kind":"theorem","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FiveTwoNinthPower.lean#L145-L154","doc":"**`Re z = (t² − 2t + 2)/2`.**  Uses `‖y₁‖² = 1/t` to turn `y₁⁻¹` into\n`t · conj y₁`, then `fiveTwoShape_re`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FiveTwoNinthPower.zz_im_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FiveTwoNinthPower.zz_im_pos","kind":"theorem","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FiveTwoNinthPower.lean#L136-L143","doc":"`Im z > 0`: `z.im = y₁.im / ‖y₁‖²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FiveTwoNinthPower.normSq_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FiveTwoNinthPower.normSq_pos","kind":"theorem","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FiveTwoNinthPower.lean#L133-L134","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FiveTwoNinthPower.normSq_mul_realRoot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FiveTwoNinthPower.normSq_mul_realRoot","kind":"theorem","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FiveTwoNinthPower.lean#L127-L131","doc":"**`‖y₁‖² · t = 1`** — read straight off the root data. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FiveTwoNinthPower.zz_pow_nine","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FiveTwoNinthPower.zz_pow_nine","kind":"theorem","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FiveTwoNinthPower.lean#L115-L119","doc":"**`z⁹ = −3z² + 4z − 2`.**  From `z³ = z − 1`: `z⁹ = (z³)³ = (z − 1)³`, and\none more reduction. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FiveTwoNinthPower.zz_cubic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FiveTwoNinthPower.zz_cubic","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FiveTwoNinthPower.lean#L106-L113","doc":"**`z³ = z − 1`.**  The Landen image of `y₁`'s cubic: clearing denominators,\n`z³ − z + 1` is exactly `(y³ − 2y² + 3y − 1) / y³`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FiveTwoNinthPower.fiveTwoShape_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FiveTwoNinthPower.fiveTwoShape_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FiveTwoNinthPower.lean#L103-L104","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FiveTwoNinthPower.zz","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FiveTwoNinthPower.zz","kind":"def","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FiveTwoNinthPower.lean#L100-L101","doc":"The third tetrahedral parameter. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FiveTwoNinthPower.ninth_power_im_pos_reduced","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FiveTwoNinthPower.ninth_power_im_pos_reduced","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FiveTwoNinthPower.lean#L84-L92","doc":"**`0 < Im (z ^ 9)`, reduced modulo the cubic.**\n\nThis is the one condition that needs the tighter bracket: it is false at\n`t = 2/5`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FiveTwoNinthPower.branch_lower","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FiveTwoNinthPower.branch_lower","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FiveTwoNinthPower.lean#L79-L82","doc":"`√3 · Im z > Re z`, i.e. `arg z > π/6` — reduced, this is\n`8(t − 1/2)² + 2 > 0`, which is unconditional. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FiveTwoNinthPower.branch_upper","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FiveTwoNinthPower.branch_upper","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FiveTwoNinthPower.lean#L72-L77","doc":"`Im z < Re z`, i.e. `arg z < π/4` — reduced, this is `−2t(t − 1) > 0`, which\nneeds only `0 < t < 1`.  Both are already proved. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FiveTwoNinthPower.realRoot_gt_three_sevenths","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FiveTwoNinthPower.realRoot_gt_three_sevenths","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FiveTwoNinthPower.lean#L59-L66","doc":"**`3/7 < realRoot`.**  Same argument as `realRoot_gt`, tighter constant:\nthe cubic is strictly increasing and `g(3/7) < 0`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}